# TLS Setup

## Domain

`app.routex.test`

## HTTPS Configuration

Nginx is configured to listen on HTTPS port `8443`.

The TLS certificate is configured in the Nginx configuration for:

`app.routex.test`

## Certificate Files

The certificate and private key are stored locally on the Nginx machine.

The private key is **NOT** included in the GitHub repository.

Certificate file:

```text
/opt/homebrew/etc/nginx/certs/routex.crt

Private key file:

/opt/homebrew/etc/nginx/certs/routex.key
Verification

HTTPS was tested using:

curl -i https://app.routex.test:8443/api/status

The response returned:

HTTP/1.1 200 OK

The response also contains:

X-Backend: A

or:

X-Backend: B

This confirms that HTTPS is successfully terminating at Nginx and requests are being forwarded to the backend servers.

TLS Handshake

The TLS communication was observed using Wireshark.

The captured TLS traffic includes:

ClientHello
ServerHello
Certificate
Change Cipher Spec
Encrypted Application Data

The final HTTPS verification was performed without using the -k certificate-validation bypass.


